# Note: the Vercel CLI only honours `.vercelignore` (plus a small built-in
# default list). Patterns in `.gitignore` are NOT applied to the upload, so
# everything that must not ship has to be listed here.

# --- Python / tooling artifacts ---
.git
.venv
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.vscode/

# --- Local database & secrets (never upload credentials) ---
db.sqlite3
*.db.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
.env.local
*.crt
*.key
*.pem

# --- Local samples / dev-only helpers ---
temp.wav
test.wav
classroom.jpg
project_init.sh
benchmark.py

# --- Source static tree (redundant in the deployment) ---
# `static/` is the Django source tree (STATICFILES_DIRS). It is collected into
# `staticfiles/`, and `vercel.json` serves `/static/(.*)` -> `/staticfiles/$1`.
# Every path in `static/` also exists in `staticfiles/`, so excluding it removes
# ~48 MiB from the upload without changing a single asset visitors receive.
# This keeps us below the Hobby plan's 100 MB static-file upload limit.
static/

# --- Repo-only docs & tooling that the runtime does not need ---
.github/
docs/
devops/
